\f[B]Portability Notes:\f[R]
.PD 0
.P
.PD
Types are \f[B]only defined when natively supported\f[R].
\f[CR]BIT128\f[R] and \f[CR]FLOAT128\f[R] depend entirely on compiler +
architecture.
On some platforms, double may be 32\-bit.
Which \f[CR]FLOAT64\f[R] will not defined.
\f[CR]SUPPORTED__BIT64\f[R] is still defined on true 64\-bit
architectures.
.RE
.PP
Always guard usage with the corresponding \f[CR]SUPPORTED__*\f[R] macro.
